# Known spyware artifact paths injected via ADB into /data/local/tmp.
#
# An unprivileged app cannot read that directory (SELinux), so androdr-020 can
# never fire here, on any device this product targets. The scenario used to
# assert "spyware file artifact" and fail as EXPECTED FAIL (#8) -- against an
# issue that closed long ago, so the harness excused a silence nobody
# re-examined (#366). Detection is not what to demand here.
#
# What is required is that the report says it could not look. A report that
# renders identically to a device where the paths WERE checked and found clean
# is the actual defect.
WHAT THIS SCAN COULD NOT CHECK
Not permitted on this device
androdr-020
could not be read on this device
# ...and a path that was never read must never be reported as clear.
!No artifact at /data/local/tmp/.raptor
